{"type":"npc","name":"Astral Flotsam","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":130,"temp":0,"max":130,"details":""},"ac":{"value":24,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"swim","value":25}],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"slashing","value":5,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"bludgeoning","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["astral","common","thalassic"],"details":"Telepathy 100 feet"},"level":{"value":7},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>When explorers desperately seek something far from home, their collective spirit of adventure occasionally takes on a life of its own in the churning seas of the Astral Plane. It matters not what they wish to find, whether it be the summit of the highest peaks, the resting place of a legendary artifact, or the threshold of a lost city, so long as their desire is strong and the task is daunting. When their quest ends in failure—either from the explorer's deaths or from circumstances forcing them to stop their search—their dream lives on. The dream drifts through the Astral Plane, carried on currents of yearning until it reaches the world from whence the explorers came. In this new realm, the dream takes on the form of an astral flotsam, a tangle of thoughts that use astral currents to propel themselves forward.</p><p>Astral flotsams remain single-mindedly devoted to achieving the quest that created them. The way they interact with others depends on the nature of their quest. They may actively seek allies or take extreme measures to ensure they are the first to reach their goal. Astral flotsams also vary significantly in how they respond to managing to reach their goal. Some choose a new, related goal they pursue with equal fervor or become stalwart allies and mentors to other explorers. However, the outcome is not always so rosy. A flotsam might become erratic and inconsolably distraught without their sense of purpose and simply fade out of existence.</p><h2>Astral Echoes</h2><p>While an astral flotsam doesn't precisely sleep, they do dream. In doing so, they exert a subtle influence on the dreams of susceptible creatures for miles around. Occasionally, a teen or young adult awakens from a strange dream in which they walk through a place of unearthly splendor and beauty—and when they describe this dream to a friend, they find the friend has had the same dream. In this way, just as an astral flotsam is born from the dreams of former heroes, they can give rise to a new generation of adventurers.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 45/100/180 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), shield, skill items (Arcana, Athletics, Nature, Occultism)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (vitality), intelligence, mind, mind shield, sensory (low-light vision), spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-anachronism.spells.yM3KTTSAIHhyuP14]{Dream Message}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Y3G6Y6EDgCY0s3fq]{Hydraulic Torrent}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Seaah9amXg70RKw2]{Water Walk}), strength, sturdy, throwing, water, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Nathan Berg","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":2},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":6},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":15,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"arcana":{"base":17},"athletics":{"base":17},"nature":{"base":15},"occultism":{"base":17}},"traits":{"value":["amphibious",